        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hydrogen, liquid, from chlorine electrolysis, production mix, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hydrogen, liquid, from chlorine electrolysis, production mix, at plant
Modul that establishs only an average of the different technologies used for hydrogen production (as co-product of chlorine) - thus no process-specific emissions are included into this dataset.;
CAS number: 001333-74-0; 
Formula: H2; 
UUID: 46aae406-7f01-391e-b980-f46ddd7814d7
Process establishing an average European hydrogen production from the three different electrolysis cell technologies (mercury, diaphragm, membrane)
Location: European average values
Technology: see general comments
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Equivalent of H2 from European Cl2 production in 2000 of 9697265 tonnes
Sampling: Official statistics from the Association of European Chlorine Producers (EuroChlor) 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_46aae406-7f01-391e-b980-f46ddd7814d7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
